  "body": "It's a common need to allow files to be dropped into \\<input type=file\\> using drag and drop on desktop browsers or tablets. Currently developers use some event handlers and javascript to do this. But a single **'droppable'** attribute would make things much easier:\r\nThe 'droppable' attribute, when added, will allow the \\<input type=file\\> and associated labels to be the drop zone. When files are dropped, the effect will be the same as the user clicked the input and selected those files.",
